{{!-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     One written page of the Notes tab.

     This exists because the decision it makes was written out eight times, and
     every one of the eight had the same bug:

         {{#if details.bio}}   <div>…the html…</div>
         {{else if unlocked}}  <textarea …></textarea>

     Read that again. The editor appears only when the field is EMPTY. A page
     could be written once and never edited afterwards — and the textarea was
     rendered with nothing between its tags anyway, so even that first write
     started from blank no matter what was already stored.

     One place now, and the rule is the other way round: unlocked, there is an
     editor, and it holds what is there; locked, the text is shown as a5e
     enriched it.

     The editor is Foundry's own rich text editor (<prose-mirror>), the one a
     journal page uses. It was a textarea handed the page as plain text, and
     what came back was wrapped in paragraphs again: bold, italics, lists,
     headings and links were gone the moment a page was edited. It edits the
     stored markup itself now, and hands it back unchanged. Saving: see the
     detail-html listener in A5eCharacterSheet.

     What is rendered is a slot holding the markup, not the editor: the sheet
     puts the editor in when the slot is first on screen. The editor's toolbar
     measures its buttons once, as it is made, and in a pane or tab that is
     not showing every button measures nothing - it came up with Format, clear,
     save and source only, no bold, no lists, no links.

     Takes:  label   the heading
             html    the field as stored
             path    where to write it, e.g. system.details.bio
             hint    placeholder for an empty one (shown by CSS)
             flat    true to leave the heading off (the four personality
                     fields sit under one shared heading)
     ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── --}}
{{#if @root.unlocked}}
  <div class="am-bio-editor-slot" data-action="detail-html"
    data-path="{{path}}" data-label="{{label}}" data-hint="{{hint}}"
    data-value="{{html}}"></div>
{{else if html}}
  <div class="am-origin-desc">{{{html}}}</div>
{{/if}}
